From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: msm: dsi: report controller state on command failure

Preserve useful controller evidence before restoring command mode on DMA
timeout: interrupt status, engine/FIFO state, clock control and command
address/length. Include the received header bytes for an invalid response.
Only existing error paths print; no additional accesses during healthy
transfers and no changes to error masks, completions or retry behavior.
Needed to distinguish missing command fetch from lost IRQ or bad BTA on
MSM8226. Register reads are from the already-powered DSI host.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 9a829eb79..bd9a71a07 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1472,10 +1472,18 @@ static int dsi_cmd_dma_tx(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, int len)
 		ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&msm_host->dma_comp,
 					msecs_to_jiffies(200));
 		DBG("ret=%d", ret);
-		if (ret == 0)
+		if (ret == 0) {
+			pr_err("%s: timeout: irq=%#x status=%#x fifo=%#x clocks=%#x dma=%#x/%u\n",
+			       __func__, dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_INTR_CTRL),
+			       dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_STATUS0),
+			       dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_FIFO_STATUS),
+			       dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CLK_CTRL),
+			       dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_DMA_BASE),
+			       dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_DMA_LEN));
 			ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
-		else
+		} else {
 			ret = len;
+		}
 	} else {
 		ret = len;
 	}
@@ -2359,7 +2367,8 @@ int msm_dsi_host_cmd_rx(struct mipi_dsi_host *host,
 		ret = dsi_long_read_resp(buf, msg);
 		break;
 	default:
-		pr_warn("%s:Invalid response cmd\n", __func__);
+		pr_warn("%s: invalid response type %#x: %*ph\n",
+			__func__, (u8)cmd, 16, buf);
 		ret = 0;
 	}
 
